  "question": {
    "text": "Consider ' $n$ ' is the number of lone pair of electrons present in the equatorial position of the most stable structure of $\\mathrm{ClF}_3$. The ions from the following with ' $n$ ' number of unpaired electrons are\nA. $\\mathrm{V}^{3+}$\nB. $\\mathrm{Ti}^{3+}$\nC. $\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$\nD. $\\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}$\nE. $\\mathrm{Ti}^{2+}$\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "kHlZA",
      "text": "A and C Only",
      "image": null,
